   "time": "Spring 53 BC",
   "narrative": "Crassus marches north from Syria with seven legions, about 4,000 light infantry and 4,000 cavalry. King Artavasdes of Armenia has twice offered troops and a route through the hills, away from the open plain; Crassus declines and takes the direct road through Mesopotamia. The guide Ariamnes urges haste and says the Parthians are weak. Modern study suggests the army kept to a busy caravan track beside the Balikh, where water was plentiful, not a waterless desert.",
